course: dictionary
lesson: 11890
title: Brilliance: clever, bright, or excellent
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Brilliance is a word with three meanings, and the sentence around it tells you which one to use. «The young coder solved the puzzle in seconds, and her brilliance amazed everyone.» Here the clues are solved and amazed, so brilliance means great cleverness or talent.
explain: «The brilliance of the stars filled the dark sky.» Stars shine, and the sky is dark, so brilliance means very bright light. Try the swap test: put "bright light" in place of brilliance and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: «Her goal in the final was a moment of brilliance.» A goal is a sports moment, and the word moment tells you that something special happened. So brilliance means the quality of being excellent or impressive, like a skilful, amazing performance.
fact: Brilliance is a noun, and it is uncountable: you say the brilliance of something, not "a brilliance" or "brilliances".
fact: «Brilliance» can mean great cleverness, such as «the brilliance of the scientist».
fact: «Brilliance» can mean very bright light or shine, such as «the brilliance of the stars».
fact: «Brilliance» can mean an excellent or impressive quality, such as «a moment of brilliance in the match».
fact: Phrases to remember: a flash of brilliance, a moment of brilliance, sheer brilliance.
exercise: «The young coder solved the puzzle in seconds, and her brilliance amazed everyone.» What does brilliance mean here? | A loud noise | Being tired after a long day | *Great cleverness or talent | Very bright light
exercise: «The brilliance of the stars filled the dark sky.» What does brilliance mean here? | Feeling sleepy | Great cleverness | Being very quiet | *Very bright light or shine
exercise: «Her goal in the final was a moment of brilliance.» What does brilliance mean here? | *The quality of being excellent or impressive | A rule of the game | A kind of ball | Bad luck
test: «The scientist's brilliance helped her find a cure for the illness.» What does brilliance mean here? | Being noisy and loud | Bad luck | *Great cleverness | Very bright light
test: «A flash of brilliance from the lamp lit up the cave.» What does brilliance mean here? | Excellent play in a game | Great cleverness | *Very bright light | Feeling calm and relaxed
exam: Which sentence uses brilliance to mean bright light? | «Her brilliance solved the maths problem first.» | *«The brilliance of the sun made us squint on the snow.» | «The team showed sheer brilliance in the final.» | «He has a brilliance for making jokes.»
